res\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[],"created_at":1793469350114246001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"628f0c2c-46b6-45be-9cdb-93dc1290fc4a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"48f1-8d72-0732-4433"}],"description":"## Goal\nMake every operator-run AWS command in rebar's own docs work as written. This deployment's AWS account (896586841071, us-east-1) is reached only through the `frontier` AWS CLI profile; an `aws` or `terraform` command run without it fails, because the default credential chain has no credentials for that account. Today only `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/README.md` passes `--profile frontier`. The other runbooks' `aws ...` commands, the Terraform runbooks (the Terraform providers pin no profile), and the local-setup TL;DR (`export AWS_PROFILE=...`) leave it out.\n\n## Scope (from a `git grep` inventory of `aws <service> <op>` across *.md and *.sh, 134 lines)\n- **Change:** every command an operator runs from their own shell in `infra/runbooks/*.md` (bedrock-access, bedrock-ci-oidc, g2p-ci-credentials, gate-scratch-mount, gerrit-auth-hardening, gerrit-host-wedged-ssm-lost, gerrit-object-store-repair, gerrit-upgrade, mcp-client-pats, provision-restore, review-bot-ops, ssm-secret-write-only, sso-auth-host) gets `--profile frontier` right after `aws <service> <op>`, including concrete inline commands such as \"`aws ssm put-parameter --overwrite …`\".\n- **Leave unchanged, with reason:**\n  - Commands that run ON the instance, which authenticates with its instance role and has no `frontier` profile; the flag would make them fail. These are the `aws bedrock-runtime converse` inside the `send-command` payload in bedrock-access.md, and every `infra/**/*.sh` script (`infra/scripts/observability.sh`, `fetch-secrets.sh`, `materialize-opcert-guard.sh`, `infra/terraform/user_data.sh`, `infra/gerrit/*.sh`).\n  - Prose that describes a command's behaviour rather than giving one to run (gerrit-host-wedged-ssm-lost.md lines 4-5, gerrit-data-volume-reclaim.md line 44).\n  - Adopter-facing docs written for other organisations' accounts (`docs/s3-backend.md`, `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md`, `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/llm-example-configs.md`), where `frontier` would be wrong for the reader.\n  - Accepted ADRs (0008, 0059, 0061), which are historical records, and `.rebar/prompts/`.\n- `AGENTS.md`: a short paragraph beside the Gerrit credential guidance. It says that every `aws` command against this deployment passes `--profile frontier` (us-east-1), that Terraform under `infra/` needs `export AWS_PROFILE=frontier` because no provider pins a profile, and that commands run on the instance take no profile.\n- `docs/local-dev-env.md` TL;DR: `export AWS_PROFILE=frontier` in place of `export AWS_PROFILE=...`.\n\n## Verification\n- A re-run of the inventory grep, filtered to `infra/runbooks/`, shows every remaining `aws <service> <op>` line without `--profile frontier` is one of the listed exclusions.\n- `make lint` passes, plus the doc-scanning tests touching AGENTS.md and docs (`pytest tests/unit -q -k \"agents_md or docs_ or runbook\"`). CI's Verified vote covers the full suite.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Every operator-shell `aws` command in `infra/runbooks/*.md` passes `--profile frontier`; the only lines without it are the listed exclusions.\n- [ ] AGENTS.md states the `--profile frontier` rule, the `AWS_PROFILE=frontier` requirement for Terraform, and the on-instance exception.\n- [ ] docs/local-dev-env.md's TL;DR exports `AWS_PROFILE=frontier`.\n- [ ] The change is merged on main with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- AGENTS.md\n- docs/local-dev-env.md\n- infra/runbooks/*.md (the 13 listed)","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"frontier profile rule"},{"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md","reason":"TL;DR AWS_PROFILE=frontier"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_secret_rotation_runbook.py","reason":"pins the runbook mirror-sync command text, now with the profile"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/bedrock-ci-oidc.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/g2p-ci-credentials.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/gate-scratch-mount.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/gerrit-auth-hardening.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/gerrit-host-wedged-ssm-lost.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/gerrit-object-store-repair.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/gerrit-upgrade.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md","reason":"--profile frontier on operator aws commands"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","48f1-8d72-0732-4433"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"670debd8-3438-447b-8e4b-618fce82de54","plan_revi